    "notes": [
      "Edge runtime: the container `supabase functions serve` creates (same image, command, mounts, env; default per_worker policy), started per run without the CLI file watcher. With NTFS last-access updates enabled, the watcher fired on worker boots and restarted the runtime mid-run, killing every open stream.",
      "Access tokens are HS256, minted with the local JWT secret (the gateway logs 'Legacy token type'); browser sessions on this stack are ES256. The handler still verifies every token with Supabase Auth getUser.",
      "Writers use POST /interviews/:id/events (the browser path) for turns and voice events, and the service-role RPCs complete_interview, request_report, save_report (the server-side path) for the terminal rows.",
      "Frame delay is client receipt minus the row's created_at, corrected by the measured database-host clock offset."
